  "goodToKnow": "Das Konservatorium is a conservatory, a music school. Leipzig's conservatory was founded by Felix Mendelssohn Bartholdy in 1843, the first in Germany. Today most have become Musikhochschulen, though the name survives in Austria and Switzerland and for some schools. A glass room on a house is der Wintergarten. Plural: die Konservatorien."
